1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,241
This also links into step number three which is all about organization and planning ahead.
这也联系到第三步：组织安排，以及提前计划。

2
00:00:04,241 --> 00:00:10,840
I really like to link this into the love language acts of service which I think is so important to give to yourself.
我喜欢把它和“服务行动”这种爱的语言联系起来，我觉得也应该很重视这样对待自己。

3
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:16,081
So an example of this that I practice is my sunday reset routine which is so important to me.
举个我自己的例子，就是我的周日整理日常，这对我很重要。

4
00:00:16,081 --> 00:00:20,120
So from 8 00 a m to 12 00 p m every single sunday so 4 hours.
每个星期天从早上八点到中午十二点，一共四个小时。

5
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:23,321
I do an entire deep clean of my apartment I do my food shop.
我会把公寓彻底打扫一遍，去买食品。

6
00:00:23,321 --> 00:00:27,601
I go for a walk and I have a workout I buy fresh flowers for my apartment.
我会出去散步、锻炼，还会买些鲜花放在公寓里。

7
00:00:27,601 --> 00:00:28,961
And I up any loose ends.
然后我会把零碎的收尾事项处理掉。

8
00:00:28,961 --> 00:00:32,081
I respond to all my text messages make sure my emails are done.
回复所有短信，确保邮件也都处理好了。

9
00:00:32,081 --> 00:00:35,791
So by midday when I'm sitting down to have my lunch the entire week I've wrapped up.
这样，到中午坐下来吃午饭的时候，我这一周的事就都收尾了。

10
00:00:35,801 --> 00:00:39,641
There is nothing lingering from this week that's going to then bother me into a new week.
没有什么这周遗留下来的事，会带进新一周继续烦着我。

11
00:00:39,641 --> 00:00:42,120
So then all of my work is going to pile up and stress me out.
这样一来，我的所有工作就会堆积起来，让我感到有压力。

12
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:45,321
Plus I'm starting monday morning on a fresh note.
另外，我星期一早上也是以一个清新的状态开始。

13
00:00:45,321 --> 00:00:52,481
I am doing myself the favor of being able to live in a clean space from monday to sunday the following week because I already took care of it.
我是在帮自己，让接下来从周一到周日都能住在干净的空间里，因为我已经提前处理好了。

14
00:00:52,481 --> 00:00:58,120
I then spend the rest of my sunday reset actually just relaxing being a couch potato watching netflix all day.
之后，周日剩下的时间我就放松，窝在沙发上整天看 Netflix。

15
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:00,881
Because I deserve that downtime and it means I'm not going to be burnt out.
因为我值得享受这些休息时间，而且她说，这意味着自己不会精疲力竭。

16
00:01:00,881 --> 00:01:08,720
When going back to work the following week during the sunday reset I also make sure I schedule and organize my week ahead in advance.
等下一周回去工作时也是这样。周日整理时，我还会确保提前安排好下一周。

17
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:10,160
And I time block everything.
我会把所有事情都分配到具体时间段里。

18
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:16,961
So I will look at my to do list my work schedule things that I want to incorporate whether it's workouts classes time with friends.
我会看看待办清单、工作日程，还有想加入的事，不管是锻炼、上课，还是跟朋友相处的时间。

19
00:01:16,961 --> 00:01:20,720
And I'm like okay monday to wednesday this is how I'm going to organize my time.
然后想，好，周一到周三，我就这样安排时间。

20
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:23,321
And it means when the week starts I don't have to think about anything.
这样一周开始时，我就不用再临时考虑什么了。

21
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:27,641
I am easily and effortlessly going through my week all of my needs are being met.
我能轻松顺畅地度过一周，各方面的需要都被照顾到。

22
00:01:27,641 --> 00:01:30,361
Because I thought about it for like 30 minutes on sunday.
原因就是我周日花了大约三十分钟提前想好了。

23
00:01:30,361 --> 00:01:34,840
And it means I am a happier individual with less stress going through every day instead.
她说，这样自己会更快乐，每天承受的压力也更小。

24
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:43,440
And let me say when it comes to scheduling and time blocking your week scheduling time for your rest your downtime your joy your time with friends and family is equally as important.
说到安排一周和划分时间段，我想强调，休息、放空、快乐，以及和亲友相处的时间，也同样重要。

25
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:48,160
Don't go overboard with I need to be working and be productive every single hour.
别过了头，觉得自己每个小时都必须工作、都必须有产出。

26
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,560
That's how you're going to burn out that's how you're going to drain yourself.
她认为，这样会让你倦怠，把自己耗空。

27
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:56,120
Self care is also about the bubble baths and the massages so make sure you're scheduling them in with this as well.
自我照顾也包括泡泡浴和按摩，所以也要确保把这些安排进去。

28
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:01,920
Step four now we know that self hair always tends to take a backseat when we get super busy in life.
第四步。我们知道，生活一忙起来，自我照顾往往就会被放到次要位置。

29
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:07,800
And why wouldn't it right who has time to do all of these extra routines every single day.
这也很自然，对吧？谁有时间每天再做这么多额外的日常步骤？

30
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:14,641
So we need to find a way to incorporate self care really quickly that's going to take no time into our every single day.
所以，我们需要找到办法，快速把自我照顾加入每天，不额外占多少时间。

31
00:02:14,641 --> 00:02:19,001
One deep breaths firsts thing in the morning when you're driving to work when you're walking somewhere.
第一，早上刚起床时、开车上班时，或者走路去某处时，做深呼吸。

32
00:02:19,001 --> 00:02:25,360
Two listening to a podcast that's going to comfort you or educate you or inspire you to set the tone for your day.
第二，听一个能安慰你、教你东西，或者激励你的播客，为这一天定下基调。

33
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:31,721
Three writing down three things you're grateful for in your notes up in journaling app on your phone when you're on your daily commute to school.
第三，在每天去学校的路上，用手机备忘录或日记应用写下三件感恩的事。

34
00:02:31,721 --> 00:02:35,600
Four indulging in your regular mundane moments.
第四，好好享受日常那些平凡的小片刻。

35
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:39,431
Your life does not have to look pretty and perfect and amazing.
你的生活不需要看上去漂亮、完美、惊艳。

36
00:02:39,441 --> 00:02:47,001
It's as simple as that one cup of coffee you have every single morning actually indulging in that moment and being completely present with it.
可以简单到每天早上那一杯咖啡，真正享受那个瞬间，全心在场。

37
00:02:47,001 --> 00:02:51,121
One thing I did actually this morning was I decided to make pancakes for breakfast.
我今天早上就做了一件这样的事，决定做松饼当早餐。

38
00:02:51,121 --> 00:02:54,920
And I make breakfast every single morning but I thought I was growing really tired of my routine.
我每天都会做早餐，但我觉得已经很厌倦这套日常了。

39
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:58,800
And I was feeling a bit meh recently and I thought let me just try and make something different.
最近我也有点提不起劲，就想，试着做点不一样的吧。

40
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:03,441
And it helped me romanticize my life it gave me joy because I was creating something.
这让我更能欣赏生活，也给我带来了快乐，因为我在创造一些东西。

41
00:03:03,441 --> 00:03:05,671
I was trying something new and it was fun.
我在尝试新鲜事，而且过程很好玩。

42
00:03:05,681 --> 00:03:09,511
And then I kind of got the reward afterwards of being able to eat the food.
之后还能吃到自己做的食物，算是一种奖励。

43
00:03:09,521 --> 00:03:17,201
And it's about changing up these little things that are a normal part of our routine every single day to inject that extra bit of joy into our day.
重点就是给每天正常重复的小事换点花样，为一天注入额外一点快乐。

44
00:03:17,201 --> 00:03:19,001
And it doesn't take up any extra time.
而且不会额外占时间。

45
00:03:19,001 --> 00:03:24,600
Another quick self care practice is changing your perspective and narrative of every moment you encounter.
另一个快速的自我照顾办法，是改变看待每个经历的角度，以及你对它的讲述方式。
